course: dictionary
lesson: 4708
title: Honorary titles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Honorary is a word for a title or job given as an honour, a way to thank or respect someone. The person does not have to pass the usual exams, do the usual work or get paid for it. The words around it give you the clues.
explain: «Edinburgh Zoo's king penguin Sir Nils Olav is an honorary officer in the Norwegian army.» A penguin cannot really train and serve in an army, so honorary tells us the title is a mark of respect, not a real job. Try your meaning in the sentence: «is a title given as an honour» still makes sense.
explain: Honorary often goes with words like degree, member and citizen, as in «honorary citizen» of a town. When you meet a new word like this, check the phrase it sits in, then ask whether the title is earned in the usual way or given to honour someone.
fact: Honorary means given as an honour, not earned in the usual way.
fact: An «honorary degree» is a title a university gives to thank or respect someone.
fact: An «honorary member» is someone who belongs to a club as a special honour.
fact: An «honorary citizen» is a title a town gives to someone to show respect.
fact: Honorary can also describe a job done without pay, such as «honorary secretary».
exercise: «Sir Nils Olav is an honorary officer in the Norwegian army.» What does honorary mean here? | Brave in battle | *Given as an honour, not the usual way | Very old and worn out | Paid a large salary every month
exercise: What is an «honorary degree»? | A cheap meal in a café | *A title a university gives to thank or respect someone | A prize for the fastest runner | Exams that every child must pass to leave school
exercise: Which job might be honorary, done without pay? | *Honorary secretary | Shop assistant on a salary | Bus driver with a monthly wage | Postman paid by the post office
test:
«The town made him an honorary citizen.» What does honorary tell us? | *A special title as a mark of respect | A job he must pay for | A passport he has lost | A house he has to rent
test:
Mia says honorary means the same as paid. Is she right? | Yes, honorary means paid well | *No, honorary means given as an honour, without the usual pay | Yes, honorary means earned by working hard for years | No, honorary means very old
exam: What is the best meaning of honorary? | A very old title from the past | A title written in gold letters | *A title given to honour someone, without the usual exams, work or pay | A title you must work hard and pass exams to win
